    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "text": "Ethereum is the global network where you control your assets, your data, and your identity.",
        "x": 350,
        "y": 896,
        "w": 741,
        "h": 78
      },
      {
        "text": "Your bank account is an entry in someone else's database. Your application is a file in someone else's server. Ethereum is an alternative network where you hold your assets directly.",
        "x": 16,
        "y": 1515,
        "w": 823,
        "h": 117
      },
      {
        "text": "322M",
        "x": 1168,
        "y": 1377,
        "w": 102,
        "h": 43
      },
      {
        "text": "ETH holders",
        "x": 1168,
        "y": 1424,
        "w": 102,
        "h": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "10 515 080",
        "x": 1168,
        "y": 1482,
        "w": 189,
        "h": 43
      },
      {
        "text": "Transactions today",
        "x": 1168,
        "y": 1529,
        "w": 189,
        "h": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "Most apps track what you do, who you talk to, and what you own. They sell that data or hand it over when asked. On Ethereum, your activity can stay private.",
        "x": 16,
        "y": 2203,
        "w": 660,
        "h": 117
      },
      {
        "text": "No account tied to your name. No company watching your balance.",
        "x": 16,
        "y": 2344,
        "w": 660,
        "h": 78
      }
